    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jpfdluy",
      "content": "Scientific names follow binomial nomenclature introduced by Carolus Linnaeus. Each organism has two names <strong>Genus</strong> (first letter capital) and <strong>Species</strong> (small letter). Names are written in italics in print and underlined separately when handwritten."
    },
